      {
        "id": 192041,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-28T20:20:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"cokeandsympathy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/a698b9/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cokeandsympathy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Okay, I apologize for the length of this log, but it was something of a slog.The last one-shot I played before the unlock was powered shock wave. I'm thinking the unlock hinges on it being played with a certain number of bots out.Unity's equipment was far in excess of the number of things Ambuscade had out at any given time, so I'm fairly certain that's not a criteria…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If anyone is still going for the unlock, I might suggest doing what I did: &nbsp;I tried to re-create Cokeandsympathy's successful unlock (referenced in the 3/21/17 post quoted above). &nbsp;By the end, I had in play 13 bots (so not all of them) and 4 equipments (2 Pylons, Volatile Parts, Workbench). &nbsp;18 cards in hand, 2 in deck, 3 in trash. &nbsp;Unfortuntately, I can't remember how long I had the bots in play, or how long they stayed out there undamaged, but I know it was a while, because I was trying to do exactly what Cokeandsympathy did on his/her last turn (destroy a Supply Crate, play Scrap Metal/Powered Shock Wave, use Workbench to play a Bee Bot, then use Scrap Metal to put another Bee Bot back in hand). &nbsp;That setup, or something very close to it, had existed for at least 1-2 turns. &nbsp;On my last turn, I:</p>\n<p>(1) Killed Ambuscade's cloaking device with Turret Bot (<em>last card he had in play</em>)</p>\n<p>(2) Played Supply Crate and Scrap Metal</p>\n<p>(3) Used Bot-Hack to destroy Supply Crate and play Bee Bot (<em>I'm not sure if I had used Bot-Hack to play a bot before, but at some point during the game, I definitely put bots in play using every method possible, including the environment (Freedom Tower)</em>)</p>\n<p>(4) Had bots try to do damage to an invisible Ambuscade</p>\n<p>(5) Used Scrap Metal to put a Bee Bot back in hand. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>…and on Ambuscade's turn, the unlock happened. &nbsp;So either (a) it was one of the actions I took on my last turn that fulfilled the unlock conditions, or (b) as of my last turn, enough of the right cards had been in play for the right number of turns to fulfill the unlock conditions. &nbsp; &nbsp;I believe people have gotten the unlock without doing any of the things I did on my last turn, so I'm leaning towards (b): &nbsp;Some number of bots/cards need to be in play for a certain number of rounds. &nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 171,
