      {
        "id": 235715,
        "name": "",
        "username": "Stenun",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/d2c977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-03-07T01:24:10.253Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello.  Sorry for Necro-ing a dead thread but I discovered something about unlocking Termi-Nation Unity that I thought worth sharing.  I’ve already posted this on the Steam forums but it makes sense to post it here, too.</p>\n<p>I unlocked Termi-Nation Unity without doing what the official unlock posted to this thread (and other guides I’ve found online) tell you to do. I did something similar but not quite the same and it worked.</p>\n<p>I didn’t mean to do it, I was trying to do what the guide said.</p>\n<p>Let me explain.</p>\n<p>I read the guide and saw that I needed to keep 5(H) Hero Targets in play for an entire round. I didn’t read any advice on how to do it; I enjoy seeing what I’ve got to do and then figuring out the How by myself. So the conclusion I reached was to use TLTachyon in the first slot, then Unity then Luminary. Just the three heroes, I planned to use Luminary’s Doomsday Device to get back loads of his devices from his trash all at the same time. I figured 15 would be easier with Unity and Luminary than making it 20 with any other Hero also in the team.</p>\n<p>So the game proceeds.<br>\nAnd I reach the point where I manage to get 15 targets in play at the end of the round. Great, now to survive the next round …<br>\nBad luck! Omnitron just did 5 damage to all Hero Targets, all Luminary’s devices die. Never mind, I still have his Doomsday Device and can get them back and try next round. Which is precisely what I do in Luminary’s turn.<br>\nAt the end of the Environment Turn … I unlock Termi-Nation Unity.</p>\n<p>So just to be clear …<br>\nI did NOT have 5(H) Hero Targets in play for an entire round.<br>\nBut I DID have 5(H) Hero Targets in play at the start of the round and 5(H) Hero Targets in play at the end of the round, too.</p>\n<p>And that was enough to get her.</p>",
        "post_number": 185,
        "post_type": 1,
